export const GUIDE = {"skill":"\n# Waypack — offline trip bundles\n\nYou are building a **trip bundle**: a small mobile web app (`index.html` + `manifest.json` + `assets/`) that the Waypack app downloads and runs **with zero network access**. The Waypack MCP server gives you `geocode`, `compute_route`, `validate_bundle`, and upload tools. The backend adds an offline vector map of the trip area automatically.\n\nWork through the phases below in order. Do not skip validation.\n\n## Phase 1 — Intake interview\n\nAsk **only what you don't already know**, in **one batched message** (numbered, short). Cover:\n\n1. Destination(s) and exact dates (and arrival/departure times if known)\n2. Travelers: adults, children's ages, mobility limits, pets\n3. Pace: relaxed / balanced / packed\n4. Interests, must-dos, must-avoids\n5. Lodging: booked? → collect name, address, confirmation #, check-in/out, phone. Not booked? → you recommend\n6. Transport: own car / rental / transit; EV? 4WD/AWD? chains?\n7. Budget level; dietary needs\n8. Season-specific gear (snow, heat, rain); connectivity expectations\n9. Preferred navigation app (Google Maps or Apple Maps)\n\nIf the user says \"just plan it\", make sensible assumptions and **list them** at the top of the Overview.\n\n## Phase 2 — Research\n\n- Research real places, current-season hours, fees, reservations, closures and seasonal risks. Prefer official sources (NPS, state DOT, operator sites).\n- **Coordinates:** call `geocode` for every place. Never guess or recall coordinates. If geocoding fails, try a more specific query (with town/state) or use `near`.\n- **Routes:** call `compute_route` for every non-trivial move (driving > ~1 km, every hike). Use `mode: \"hiking\"` for trails. Paste the returned `geometry`, `distance_m`, `duration_s` into the manifest.\n- Volatile facts (road conditions, chain controls, weather, closures) are **never** stated as fact: say \"verify before leaving\" and add a `live_checks` link.\n\n## Phase 3 — Author the bundle\n\nStart from the template: CLI agents run `npx @waypack/cli init ./waypack/<slug>` (or copy `templates/base/` from this skill). Chat agents call `get_authoring_guide` and reproduce the template files.\n\n1. **`manifest.json`** — structured data, the source of truth for the app's native Today view, notifications and the offline map. Schema: `reference/manifest.md`. Key rules:\n   - `places[].id` / `routes[].id`: lowercase slugs (`lodge-wuksachi`, `r-day1-drive`)\n   - `map.bbox` = `[minLon, minLat, maxLon, maxLat]` covering every place + a few km. ≤ 40,000 km² per box; use `extra_areas` (≤ 3 more) for far-apart bases instead of one giant box.\n   - Every day between `start_date` and `end_date` gets a `days[]` entry; items sorted by `time` (24h `HH:MM`, local to `timezone`).\n   - Set `nav_app` to `\"google\"` or `\"apple\"` from the interview.\n2. **`index.html`** — the rich experience. Keep the template's tabs (Today / Plan / Map / Places / Guide); rewrite the **Guide** section content with your research. Add per-day rich notes via `<div data-day-notes=\"YYYY-MM-DD\">`. You may restyle or restructure freely, as long as the rules in `reference/authoring.md` hold.\n3. **Coverage checklist** — every plan must address each item (or say \"N/A — reason\"):\n   - [ ] **Overview**: one-screen summary, dates, travelers, key reservations, assumptions\n   - [ ] **Today view** reachable in one tap (template's Today tab)\n   - [ ] **Day-by-day itinerary** with times, durations, buffers; drive times from `compute_route`\n   - [ ] **Lodging**: address, coordinates, check-in/out, confirmation #, phone, parking\n   - [ ] **Routes**: every non-trivial move, with notes (closures, chains, tolls, last fuel)\n   - [ ] **Places**: hours (\"verify\"), cost, reservation needs, kid/accessibility notes\n   - [ ] **Food** near each day's area, plus a fallback if closed\n   - [ ] **Conditions & live checks**: seasonal risks + `live_checks` links\n   - [ ] **Safety**: no-service zones, emergency numbers, nearest hospital/urgent care, ranger stations (as `medical`/`other` places referenced from `emergency.places`)\n   - [ ] **Packing list** for season, activities, travelers\n   - [ ] **Budget** estimate by category\n   - [ ] **Backup plans** per day for weather/closures\n   - [ ] **Offline prep**: download trip in Waypack, download Google/Apple offline area, charge power banks, print confirmations\n\n### Hard rules (the validator enforces them)\n- **No network.** Every `src`/`href` for scripts, styles, images, fonts must be a relative path in the bundle, a `data:` URI, or `/__waypack/sdk/v1/…`. No CDNs, no Google Fonts, no remote images, no iframes, no `<base>`. External `<a href=\"https://…\">` links are fine (they open the browser when online).\n- Include the SDK: `<script src=\"/__waypack/sdk/v1/waypack.js\"></script>`. Use `Waypack.map()` for maps — never bundle MapLibre/Leaflet or tile URLs.\n- Every place/item gets a **Navigate** button → `Waypack.openInMaps(placeId)`.\n- Mobile-first: tap targets ≥ 44px, body text ≥ 16px, works one-handed, supports dark mode (`prefers-color-scheme`).\n- ≤ 25 MB zipped, ≤ 2,000 files; images WebP/JPEG ≤ 1600px. Prefer inline SVG.\n\nSDK reference: `reference/sdk.md`.\n\n## Phase 4 — Validate (required)\n\n- CLI: `npx @waypack/cli validate ./waypack/<slug>` — fix **all errors**; fix warnings unless you have a reason (state it to the user).\n- Or MCP `validate_bundle` with the files.\n- Optional: `npx @waypack/cli preview ./waypack/<slug>` and check it in a phone-sized browser.\n\n## Phase 5 — Upload\n\nSee `reference/upload.md`. Summary:\n- **CLI agents:** `npx @waypack/cli zip ./waypack/<slug> -o bundle.zip` → MCP `create_upload {size_bytes}` → `curl -fsS -X PUT -T bundle.zip \"<put_url>\"` → MCP `finalize_upload {upload_id}`.\n- **Chat agents (no shell):** MCP `upload_bundle_inline` with `files: [{path, content, encoding}]` (utf-8 text, base64 binary; ≤ 4 MB total).\n- **Updating** a trip: set `manifest.trip_id` to the existing id (from `list_trips` / the first upload) and upload again → new version. Use `get_trip` to fetch the current manifest first.\n\nThen call `get_trip_status` until `status` is `ready` (map extraction takes ~1–3 min) and tell the user:\n> \"Open Waypack on your phone and tap **Download** on *<title>* before you lose signal.\"\n\nIf the server returns an entitlement/limit message, relay it verbatim — don't retry in a loop.\n","references":{"authoring.md":"# Authoring rules & design guidance\n\n## Layout\n```\n<slug>/\n  manifest.json   # required\n  index.html      # required entry point\n  assets/         # css, js, images, fonts — all local\n```\n\n## Must (validator errors)\n- `src`/`href` for `<script>`, `<link>`, `<img>`/`srcset`, `<source>`, `<video>`, `<audio>`, CSS `url()`/`@import`: relative path that exists in the bundle, `data:`/`blob:`, or `/__waypack/sdk/v1/…`.\n- No `<iframe>`, `<base>`, `<meta http-equiv=refresh>`, external `<form action>`, or ES module imports from URLs.\n- No absolute paths other than the SDK (`/assets/x.css` breaks — write `assets/x.css`).\n- No `..`, absolute paths, or symlinks in the zip. ≤ 25 MB zipped, ≤ 2,000 files.\n\n## Runtime CSP (set by the app)\n```\ndefault-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';\nimg-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self';\nworker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'\n```\n`fetch()` only works for files inside the bundle. Embed data in `manifest.json` or a local `.json`.\n\n## Should (validator warnings)\n- Viewport meta; dark mode via `prefers-color-scheme`.\n- Sections for packing, budget, emergency, backup plans; Navigate buttons via `Waypack.openInMaps`.\n- `live_checks` and `emergency.numbers` present.\n\n## Design\n- Readable at arm's length: body ≥ 16px, high contrast, generous spacing.\n- One-handed: primary actions at the bottom, tap targets ≥ 44px, no hover-only UI.\n- \"What's next\" is one tap away (Today tab). Times in local 12h/24h per locale.\n- Use system fonts (no font downloads); inline SVG icons or emoji.\n- Long content in `<details>`; tables only for budgets.\n- Checklists can persist ticks with `localStorage` (per device).\n- Images: WebP/JPEG ≤ 1600px, ≤ 300 KB each; only when they add real value (e.g. a trail junction photo).\n- Never present volatile conditions as fact. Say \"verify\" and link a live check.\n- Write for someone tired, cold and offline: exact names, addresses, confirmation numbers, what to do if X is closed.\n","manifest.md":"# manifest.json (schema v1)\n\nAuthoritative JSON Schema: `packages/bundle-schema/manifest.v1.schema.json` (also returned by the MCP `get_authoring_guide` tool).\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,               // always 1\n  \"sdk_version\": \"1\",                // SDK major the bundle targets\n  \"trip_id\": null,                   // null = new trip; existing UUID = publish a new version\n  \"title\": \"Sequoia Winter Weekend\", // ≤ 120 chars\n  \"summary\": \"3 days in Sequoia with a toddler…\",\n  \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", // IANA; all times are local to it\n  \"start_date\": \"2026-12-24\",        // YYYY-MM-DD\n  \"end_date\": \"2026-12-26\",\n  \"travelers\": { \"adults\": 2, \"children\": [{ \"age\": 2 }] },\n  \"nav_app\": \"google\",               // optional: \"google\" | \"apple\" (default by platform)\n  \"map\": {\n    \"bbox\": [-118.95, 36.40, -118.55, 36.80], // [minLon, minLat, maxLon, maxLat], ≤ 40,000 km²\n    \"max_zoom\": 15,                            // 10–16 (basemap detail tops out at 15)\n    \"extra_areas\": [ { \"bbox\": [...], \"label\": \"Fresno\" } ] // ≤ 3 more boxes\n  },\n  \"places\": [{\n    \"id\": \"lodge-wuksachi\",          // ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$, unique across places\n    \"name\": \"Wuksachi Lodge\",\n    \"category\": \"lodging\",           // lodging|food|sight|activity|trailhead|transport|fuel|shopping|medical|other\n    \"lat\": 36.5960, \"lon\": -118.7547,// from `geocode` — never guessed\n    \"address\": \"...\", \"phone\": \"+1-...\", \"hours\": \"...\", \"cost\": \"...\",\n    \"notes\": \"Check-in 4pm. Confirmation #ABC123.\",\n    \"links\": [{ \"label\": \"Reservation\", \"url\": \"https://...\" }]  // http(s)/tel/mailto/sms\n  }],\n  \"routes\": [{\n    \"id\": \"r-day1-drive\",\n    \"name\": \"Three Rivers → Wuksachi Lodge\",\n    \"mode\": \"driving\",               // driving|walking|hiking|cycling|transit|ferry|flight\n    \"from\": \"place-three-rivers\", \"to\": \"lodge-wuksachi\",   // optional place ids\n    \"distance_m\": 52000, \"duration_s\": 4500,\n    \"geometry\": { \"type\": \"LineString\", \"coordinates\": [[lon, lat], ...] }, // from `compute_route`, ≤ 5,000 points\n    \"notes\": \"Chains may be required — verify.\"\n  }],\n  \"days\": [{\n    \"date\": \"2026-12-24\", \"title\": \"Drive in & Giant Forest\", \"notes\": \"optional\",\n    \"items\": [{\n      \"time\": \"09:00\", \"end_time\": \"10:30\",   // 24h HH:MM; items sorted by time\n      \"title\": \"Drive to park entrance\",\n      \"place_id\": \"place-three-rivers\", \"route_id\": \"r-day1-drive\",\n      \"kind\": \"travel\",                        // travel|activity|meal|lodging|rest|reservation|other\n      \"notes\": \"Last gas in Three Rivers.\"\n    }]\n  }],\n  \"live_checks\": [{ \"label\": \"Caltrans road conditions\", \"url\": \"https://quickmap.dot.ca.gov/\" }],\n  \"emergency\": {\n    \"numbers\": [{ \"label\": \"Emergency\", \"value\": \"911\" }],\n    \"notes\": \"Most of the park has no cell service…\",\n    \"places\": [\"hospital-kaweah\"]              // place ids\n  },\n  \"offline_notes\": \"Download a Google Maps offline area for Visalia–Sequoia.\"\n}\n```\n\n## Integrity rules checked by the validator\n- Referenced ids (`place_id`, `route_id`, `from`, `to`, `emergency.places`) must exist.\n- `start_date ≤ end_date`; every `days[].date` within range and unique; a warning for missing days.\n- Items sorted by `time`; `end_time ≥ time` (split overnight items across days).\n- Places outside every map area → warning with a suggested expanded bbox.\n- Route geometry: valid `[lon, lat]` order, ≤ 5,000 coordinates; 2-point lines get a warning (use `compute_route`).\n- Extra properties are allowed (for your own rendering) — the app ignores them.\n","sdk.md":"# Waypack SDK v1 (`window.Waypack`)\n\nInclude once, before your own scripts:\n\n```html\n<script src=\"/__waypack/sdk/v1/waypack.js\"></script>\n```\n\nThe app serves it locally (offline); `waypack preview` serves it too. In a plain browser without the SDK, `window.Waypack` is undefined — guard with `if (window.Waypack)`.\n\n```ts\nWaypack.version: string\nWaypack.manifest(): Promise<Manifest>           // parsed manifest.json (cached)\nWaypack.isOnline(): boolean\nWaypack.platform(): \"ios\" | \"android\" | \"web\"\n\nWaypack.map(container: HTMLElement | string, opts?: {\n  places?: string[] | \"all\";        // default all (or the day's)\n  routes?: string[] | \"all\";\n  day?: string;                     // \"YYYY-MM-DD\": only that day's places/routes\n  fit?: \"places\" | \"routes\" | \"bbox\";\n  showUserLocation?: boolean;       // default true — GPS blue dot works offline\n  interactive?: boolean;            // default true\n  style?: \"light\" | \"dark\" | \"auto\";// default auto (follows system)\n  onPlaceClick?: (placeId) => void; // default: popup with a Navigate button\n}): Promise<TripMap>\n\nTripMap.flyTo(placeId, zoom?)       // pans + opens the popup\nTripMap.highlightRoute(routeId|null)// emphasizes one route and fits to it\nTripMap.setDay(date|null)           // filter to a day (null = all)\nTripMap.destroy()\nTripMap.raw                         // maplibregl.Map escape hatch (not semver-stable)\n\nWaypack.openInMaps(placeId | {lat, lon, label?}, { app?: \"google\"|\"apple\"|\"auto\", navigate?: true })\nWaypack.openExternal(url)           // system browser\nWaypack.share(text)                 // native share sheet\n\nWaypack.categories                  // { lodging: {color, emoji, label}, … } for consistent styling\nWaypack.routeModes                  // { driving: {color, dash?, label}, … }\n```\n\n## Notes\n- The map container needs an explicit height (e.g. `height: 60vh`).\n- Basemap: OpenStreetMap vector tiles cut to `map.bbox` (+ `extra_areas`). Outside them the map is blank offline. Attribution is shown automatically — don't hide it.\n- Routes are styled by mode (hiking dashed, driving solid); places by category.\n- Don't create maps for hidden elements; create on first show (see template `ensureMap`).\n- One map per page is plenty; call `destroy()` before creating another in the same container.\n","upload.md":"# Uploading a bundle\n\nAll tools are on the Waypack MCP server (`https://mcp.waypack.app/mcp`). Sign-in happens via OAuth the first time a tool is used.\n\n## CLI agents (filesystem + shell)\n1. `npx @waypack/cli validate ./waypack/<slug>` → fix errors.\n2. `npx @waypack/cli zip ./waypack/<slug> -o ./waypack/<slug>.zip` (prints `size_bytes`).\n3. MCP `create_upload { \"trip_id\"?: \"<uuid for updates>\", \"size_bytes\": <n> }` → `{ upload_id, put_url, expires_at }`.\n4. `curl -fsS -X PUT -H \"Content-Type: application/zip\" -T ./waypack/<slug>.zip \"<put_url>\"`\n5. MCP `finalize_upload { \"upload_id\": \"<id>\" }` → `{ trip_id, version, status, app_hint }`.\n6. MCP `get_trip_status { \"trip_id\" }` until `status: \"ready\"`.\n\nIf `finalize_upload` returns validation errors, fix, re-zip, and repeat from step 3 (upload ids are single-use).\n\n## Chat agents (no shell)\n`upload_bundle_inline { \"trip_id\"?: \"...\", \"files\": [ { \"path\": \"manifest.json\", \"content\": \"{...}\", \"encoding\": \"utf-8\" }, { \"path\": \"assets/photo.webp\", \"content\": \"<base64>\", \"encoding\": \"base64\" } ] }`\n- ≤ 4 MB total. Prefer inline SVG and few/no photos.\n- Same response as `finalize_upload`.\n\n## Updating\n- `list_trips` → find the trip; `get_trip { trip_id }` → current manifest.\n- Set `manifest.trip_id` to that id, change what's needed, upload again. The app shows \"Update available\".\n- Map tiles are re-cut only if `map` changed.\n\n## Limits (free tier)\nFree accounts get 1 active trip and no offline map extract (the map needs a connection). If a tool returns a limit message, show it to the user; don't retry.\n"},"template":{"assets/app.js":"/* Waypack base template — renders Today / Plan / Map / Places from manifest.json.\n * The Guide tab is hand-authored HTML in index.html. No network access, no dependencies\n * besides the Waypack SDK (window.Waypack), which may be absent in a plain browser. */\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  var W = window.Waypack || null;\n  var M = null; // manifest\n  var placesById = {};\n  var routesById = {};\n  var tripMap = null;\n  var mapLoading = null;\n\n  // ---------- helpers ----------\n  function esc(s) {\n    return String(s == null ? \"\" : s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, function (c) {\n      return { \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\", \"'\": \"&#39;\" }[c];\n    });\n  }\n  function $(sel, root) { return (root || document).querySelector(sel); }\n  function $all(sel, root) { return Array.prototype.slice.call((root || document).querySelectorAll(sel)); }\n\n  var CATS = (W && W.categories) || {\n    lodging: { color: \"#7c3aed\", emoji: \"🛏️\", label: \"Lodging\" }, food: { color: \"#ea580c\", emoji: \"🍴\", label: \"Food\" },\n    sight: { color: \"#0891b2\", emoji: \"📷\", label: \"Sight\" }, activity: { color: \"#16a34a\", emoji: \"⭐\", label: \"Activity\" },\n    trailhead: { color: \"#15803d\", emoji: \"🥾\", label: \"Trailhead\" }, transport: { color: \"#2563eb\", emoji: \"🚌\", label: \"Transport\" },\n    fuel: { color: \"#ca8a04\", emoji: \"⛽\", label: \"Fuel\" }, shopping: { color: \"#db2777\", emoji: \"🛒\", label: \"Shopping\" },\n    medical: { color: \"#dc2626\", emoji: \"🏥\", label: \"Medical\" }, other: { color: \"#64748b\", emoji: \"📍\", label: \"Other\" }\n  };\n  var KIND = { travel: \"Travel\", activity: \"Activity\", meal: \"Meal\", lodging: \"Lodging\", rest: \"Rest\", reservation: \"Reservation\", other: \"\" };\n\n  /** Current date/time in the trip's time zone, as strings comparable with the manifest. */\n  function nowInTz(tz) {\n    try {\n      var parts = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(\"en-CA\", {\n        timeZone: tz, year: \"numeric\", month: \"2-digit\", day: \"2-digit\", hour: \"2-digit\", minute: \"2-digit\", hourCycle: \"h23\"\n      }).formatToParts(new Date());\n      var p = {};\n      parts.forEach(function (x) { p[x.type] = x.value; });\n      return { date: p.year + \"-\" + p.month + \"-\" + p.day, time: p.hour + \":\" + p.minute };\n    } catch (e) {\n      var d = new Date();\n      return { date: d.toISOString().slice(0, 10), time: d.toTimeString().slice(0, 5) };\n    }\n  }\n  function parseDate(s) { var a = s.split(\"-\"); return new Date(Date.UTC(+a[0], +a[1] - 1, +a[2], 12)); }\n  function fmtDate(s, opts) {\n    return parseDate(s).toLocaleDateString(undefined, Object.assign({ timeZone: \"UTC\", weekday: \"short\", month: \"short\", day: \"numeric\" }, opts || {}));\n  }\n  function fmtTime(t) {\n    if (!t) return \"\";\n    var h = +t.slice(0, 2), m = t.slice(3, 5);\n    var d = new Date(Date.UTC(2000, 0, 1, h, +m));\n    return d.toLocaleTimeString(undefined, { timeZone: \"UTC\", hour: \"numeric\", minute: \"2-digit\" });\n  }\n  function daysBetween(a, b) { return Math.round((parseDate(b) - parseDate(a)) / 86400000); }\n  function fmtDuration(s) {\n    if (!s) return \"\";\n    var h = Math.floor(s / 3600), m = Math.round((s % 3600) / 60);\n    return h ? h + \" h \" + (m ? m + \" min\" : \"\") : m + \" min\";\n  }\n  function fmtDistance(m) {\n    if (!m) return \"\";\n    var imperial = /^en-US/.test(navigator.language);\n    return imperial ? (m / 1609.34).toFixed(m < 16000 ? 1 : 0) + \" mi\" : (m / 1000).toFixed(m < 10000 ? 1 : 0) + \" km\";\n  }\n\n  function navButton(placeId, cls) {\n    return placeId && placesById[placeId]\n      ? '<button class=\"btn ' + (cls || \"small\") + '\" data-nav=\"' + esc(placeId) + '\">Navigate</button>' : \"\";\n  }\n  function mapButton(item) {\n    if (item.route_id && routesById[item.route_id]) return '<button class=\"btn small secondary\" data-route=\"' + esc(item.route_id) + '\">Route</button>';\n    if (item.place_id && placesById[item.place_id]) return '<button class=\"btn small secondary\" data-show=\"' + esc(item.place_id) + '\">Map</button>';\n    return \"\";\n  }\n\n  // ---------- tabs ----------\n  var TABS = [\"today\", \"plan\", \"map\", \"places\", \"guide\"];\n  function showTab(name) {\n    if (TABS.indexOf(name) < 0) name = \"today\";\n    $all(\".tab\").forEach(function (el) { el.hidden = el.getAttribute(\"data-tab\") !== name; });\n    $all(\".tabbar a\").forEach(function (a) {\n      if (a.getAttribute(\"data-go\") === name) a.setAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\"); else a.removeAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n    });\n    if (name === \"map\") ensureMap();\n    window.scrollTo(0, 0);\n  }\n  function route() {\n    var h = (location.hash || \"#today\").slice(1);\n    if (TABS.indexOf(h) >= 0) return showTab(h);\n    // Deep link to a guide section, e.g. #g-packing\n    var target = h && document.getElementById(h);\n    if (target) {\n      var tab = target.closest(\".tab\");\n      if (tab) showTab(tab.getAttribute(\"data-tab\"));\n      target.scrollIntoView();\n    } else showTab(\"today\");\n  }\n\n  // ---------- map ----------\n  function ensureMap() {\n    if (mapLoading) return mapLoading;\n    if (!W) {\n      $(\"#map\").innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Maps need the Waypack app (or <code>waypack preview</code>).</p>';\n      return (mapLoading = Promise.resolve(null));\n    }\n    mapLoading = W.map(\"#map\", { fit: \"bbox\" }).then(function (m) { tripMap = m; return m; }).catch(function (e) {\n      console.error(e);\n      $(\"#map\").innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Map could not load: ' + esc(e.message) + \"</p>\";\n      return null;\n    });\n    return mapLoading;\n  }\n  function onMap(fn) {\n    location.hash = \"#map\";\n    ensureMap().then(function (m) { if (m) setTimeout(function () { fn(m); }, 50); });\n  }\n\n  // ---------- renderers ----------\n  function itemHtml(it, state) {\n    var p = it.place_id && placesById[it.place_id];\n    var r = it.route_id && routesById[it.route_id];\n    var meta = [];\n    if (r) meta.push([fmtDistance(r.distance_m), fmtDuration(r.duration_s)].filter(Boolean).join(\" · \"));\n    if (p && !r) meta.push(p.name);\n    return '<li class=\"item ' + (state || \"\") + '\">' +\n      '<div class=\"time\">' + (it.time ? esc(fmtTime(it.time)) : \"—\") + (it.end_time ? \"<small>\" + esc(fmtTime(it.end_time)) + \"</small>\" : \"\") + \"</div>\" +\n      \"<div>\" + (it.kind && KIND[it.kind] ? '<span class=\"tag\">' + esc(KIND[it.kind]) + \"</span>\" : \"\") +\n      \"<h3>\" + esc(it.title) + \"</h3>\" +\n      (meta.filter(Boolean).length ? '<p class=\"meta\">' + esc(meta.filter(Boolean).join(\" · \")) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n      (it.notes ? \"<p>\" + esc(it.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n      (r && r.notes ? '<p class=\"callout\">' + esc(r.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n      '<div class=\"btn-row\">' + navButton(it.place_id || (r && r.to)) + mapButton(it) + \"</div>\" +\n      \"</div></li>\";\n  }\n\n  function renderToday() {\n    var el = $(\"#tab-today\");\n    var now = nowInTz(M.timezone);\n    var html = \"\";\n    var days = M.days.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return a.date < b.date ? -1 : 1; });\n\n    if (now.date < M.start_date) {\n      var n = daysBetween(now.date, M.start_date);\n      html += '<article class=\"card hero\"><div class=\"label\">Coming up</div><h2>' + (n === 1 ? \"Tomorrow\" : n + \" days to go\") + \"</h2>\" +\n        '<div class=\"when\">' + esc(fmtDate(M.start_date)) + \" – \" + esc(fmtDate(M.end_date)) + \"</div>\" +\n        (M.summary ? \"<p>\" + esc(M.summary) + \"</p>\" : \"\") + \"</article>\";\n      html += '<article class=\"card\"><h2>Before you go</h2><p>Make sure this trip says <b>Available offline</b> in the Waypack app, and work through the <a href=\"#g-offline\">offline prep checklist</a>.</p></article>';\n      if (days[0]) html += '<h2 class=\"muted\" style=\"padding:0 4px\">Day 1 · ' + esc(days[0].title || fmtDate(days[0].date)) + '</h2><ul class=\"items\">' + days[0].items.map(function (it) { return itemHtml(it); }).join(\"\") + \"</ul>\";\n    } else if (now.date > M.end_date) {\n      html += '<article class=\"card hero\"><div class=\"label\">Trip complete</div><h2>' + esc(M.title) + '</h2><div class=\"when\">' + esc(fmtDate(M.start_date)) + \" – \" + esc(fmtDate(M.end_date)) + \"</div></article>\";\n      html += '<p class=\"empty\">Browse the full plan in the <a href=\"#plan\">Plan</a> tab.</p>';\n    } else {\n      var day = days.filter(function (d) { return d.date === now.date; })[0];\n      var dayNum = daysBetween(M.start_date, now.date) + 1;\n      if (!day || !day.items.length) {\n        html += '<article class=\"card hero\"><div class=\"label\">Day ' + dayNum + '</div><h2>' + esc((day && day.title) || \"Free day\") + \"</h2><p>Nothing scheduled — enjoy it.</p></article>\";\n      } else {\n        var items = day.items;\n        var idxNow = -1, idxNext = -1;\n        items.forEach(function (it, i) {\n          if (!it.time) return;\n          var end = it.end_time || (items[i + 1] && items[i + 1].time) || \"23:59\";\n          if (it.time <= now.time && now.time < end) idxNow = i;\n          if (idxNext < 0 && it.time > now.time) idxNext = i;\n        });\n        var focus = idxNow >= 0 ? idxNow : idxNext;\n        var f = items[focus];\n        if (f) {\n          var fp = f.place_id && placesById[f.place_id];\n          html += '<article class=\"card hero\"><div class=\"label\">' + (focus === idxNow ? \"Now\" : \"Next up\") + \" · Day \" + dayNum + \"</div>\" +\n            \"<h2>\" + esc(f.title) + '</h2><div class=\"when\">' + esc(fmtTime(f.time)) + (f.end_time ? \" – \" + esc(fmtTime(f.end_time)) : \"\") + (fp ? \" · \" + esc(fp.name) : \"\") + \"</div>\" +\n            (f.notes ? \"<p>\" + esc(f.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n            '<div class=\"btn-row\">' + navButton(f.place_id || (f.route_id && routesById[f.route_id] && routesById[f.route_id].to), \"\") + \"</div></article>\";\n        } else {\n          html += '<article class=\"card hero\"><div class=\"label\">Day ' + dayNum + '</div><h2>All done for today</h2><p>' + esc(day.title || \"\") + \"</p></article>\";\n        }\n        html += '<div class=\"day-head\"><h2>' + esc(day.title || \"Today\") + '</h2><span class=\"muted\">' + esc(fmtDate(day.date)) + \"</span></div>\";\n        html += '<ul class=\"items\">' + items.map(function (it, i) {\n          var st = i === idxNow ? \"now\" : (it.time && (it.end_time || (items[i + 1] && items[i + 1].time) || \"23:59\") <= now.time ? \"done\" : \"\");\n          return itemHtml(it, st);\n        }).join(\"\") + \"</ul>\";\n      }\n    }\n    var lodging = M.places.filter(function (p) { return p.category === \"lodging\"; });\n    if (lodging.length) {\n      html += '<article class=\"card\"><h2>Where you\\'re staying</h2>' + lodging.map(function (p) {\n        return \"<p><b>\" + esc(p.name) + \"</b><br>\" + esc(p.address || \"\") + (p.notes ? '<br><span class=\"muted\">' + esc(p.notes) + \"</span>\" : \"\") + '</p><div class=\"btn-row\">' + navButton(p.id) + (p.phone ? '<a class=\"btn small secondary\" href=\"tel:' + esc(p.phone) + '\">Call</a>' : \"\") + \"</div>\";\n      }).join(\"\") + \"</article>\";\n    }\n    html += '<div class=\"btn-row\"><a class=\"btn secondary\" href=\"#g-safety\">Emergency info</a><a class=\"btn secondary\" href=\"#map\">Map</a></div>';\n    el.innerHTML = html;\n  }\n\n  function renderPlan() {\n    var notes = {};\n    $all(\"[data-day-notes]\").forEach(function (n) { notes[n.getAttribute(\"data-day-notes\")] = n.innerHTML; });\n    var today = nowInTz(M.timezone).date;\n    $(\"#tab-plan\").innerHTML = M.days.map(function (d, i) {\n      return '<section class=\"day\" id=\"day-' + esc(d.date) + '\"><div class=\"day-head\"><h2>Day ' + (i + 1) + \" · \" + esc(d.title || \"\") + \"</h2>\" +\n        '<span class=\"muted\">' + esc(fmtDate(d.date)) + (d.date === today ? \" · Today\" : \"\") + \"</span></div>\" +\n        (d.notes ? '<p class=\"day-notes\">' + esc(d.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n        (notes[d.date] ? '<div class=\"day-notes\">' + notes[d.date] + \"</div>\" : \"\") +\n        '<ul class=\"items\">' + (d.items.length ? d.items.map(function (it) { return itemHtml(it); }).join(\"\") : '<li class=\"empty\">Free time</li>') + \"</ul>\" +\n        '<button class=\"btn small secondary\" data-day-map=\"' + esc(d.date) + '\">Show day ' + (i + 1) + \" on map</button></section>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n  }\n\n  var placeFilter = \"all\";\n  function renderPlaces() {\n    var cats = [];\n    M.places.forEach(function (p) { if (cats.indexOf(p.category) < 0) cats.push(p.category); });\n    var html = '<div class=\"filters\" role=\"toolbar\">' + [\"all\"].concat(cats).map(function (c) {\n      return '<button data-filter=\"' + esc(c) + '\" aria-pressed=\"' + (c === placeFilter) + '\">' + esc(c === \"all\" ? \"All\" : (CATS[c] || CATS.other).label) + \"</button>\";\n    }).join(\"\") + \"</div>\";\n    html += M.places.filter(function (p) { return placeFilter === \"all\" || p.category === placeFilter; }).map(function (p) {\n      var c = CATS[p.category] || CATS.other;\n      return '<article class=\"card place\" id=\"place-' + esc(p.id) + '\"><div class=\"dot\" style=\"background:' + c.color + '22\" aria-hidden=\"true\">' + c.emoji + \"</div><div>\" +\n        \"<h3>\" + esc(p.name) + '</h3><div class=\"meta\">' + esc([c.label, p.hours, p.cost].filter(Boolean).join(\" · \")) + \"</div>\" +\n        (p.address ? '<div class=\"meta\">' + esc(p.address) + \"</div>\" : \"\") +\n        (p.notes ? \"<p>\" + esc(p.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n        (p.links || []).map(function (l) { return '<a href=\"' + esc(l.url) + '\">' + esc(l.label) + \" ↗</a> \"; }).join(\"\") +\n        '<div class=\"btn-row\">' + navButton(p.id) + '<button class=\"btn small secondary\" data-show=\"' + esc(p.id) + '\">Map</button>' +\n        (p.phone ? '<a class=\"btn small secondary\" href=\"tel:' + esc(p.phone) + '\">Call</a>' : \"\") + \"</div></div></article>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    $(\"#tab-places\").innerHTML = html;\n  }\n\n  function renderGuide() {\n    var lc = $(\"#live-checks\");\n    if (lc) lc.innerHTML = (M.live_checks || []).map(function (l) { return '<a href=\"' + esc(l.url) + '\">' + esc(l.label) + \"</a>\"; }).join(\"\") || '<p class=\"muted\">No live checks listed.</p>';\n    var em = $(\"#emergency\");\n    if (em && M.emergency) {\n      var e = M.emergency;\n      em.innerHTML = (e.numbers || []).map(function (n) {\n        return '<div class=\"emergency-num\"><span>' + esc(n.label) + '</span><a href=\"tel:' + esc(n.value.replace(/[^+\\d]/g, \"\")) + '\">' + esc(n.value) + \"</a></div>\";\n      }).join(\"\") + (e.notes ? '<p class=\"callout\">' + esc(e.notes) + \"</p>\" : \"\") +\n        (e.places || []).map(function (id) {\n          var p = placesById[id];\n          return p ? \"<p><b>\" + esc(p.name) + \"</b><br>\" + esc(p.address || \"\") + '</p><div class=\"btn-row\">' + navButton(id) + (p.phone ? '<a class=\"btn small secondary\" href=\"tel:' + esc(p.phone) + '\">Call</a>' : \"\") + \"</div>\" : \"\";\n        }).join(\"\");\n    }\n    // Checklists remember ticks on this device.\n    $all(\".checklist\").forEach(function (ul) {\n      var key = \"wp:\" + M.title + \":\" + (ul.getAttribute(\"data-store\") || \"list\");\n      var saved = {};\n      try { saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || \"{}\"); } catch (e) { /* storage unavailable */ }\n      $all(\"li\", ul).forEach(function (li, i) {\n        if (saved[i]) li.classList.add(\"checked\");\n        li.setAttribute(\"role\", \"checkbox\");\n        li.setAttribute(\"aria-checked\", String(!!saved[i]));\n        li.tabIndex = 0;\n        li.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n          saved[i] = !saved[i];\n          li.classList.toggle(\"checked\", saved[i]);\n          li.setAttribute(\"aria-checked\", String(saved[i]));\n          try { localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(saved)); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n        });\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  function renderMapDays() {\n    var sel = $(\"#map-day\");\n    sel.innerHTML = '<option value=\"\">All days</option>' + M.days.map(function (d, i) {\n      return '<option value=\"' + esc(d.date) + '\">Day ' + (i + 1) + \" · \" + esc(d.title || fmtDate(d.date)) + \"</option>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    sel.addEventListener(\"change\", function () { ensureMap().then(function (m) { if (m) m.setDay(sel.value || null); }); });\n  }\n\n  // ---------- events ----------\n  document.addEventListener(\"click\", function (e) {\n    var t = e.target.closest(\"[data-nav],[data-show],[data-route],[data-day-map],[data-filter],a[href^='http']\");\n    if (!t) return;\n    if (t.hasAttribute(\"data-nav\")) {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      var id = t.getAttribute(\"data-nav\");\n      if (W) W.openInMaps(id);\n      else { var p = placesById[id]; window.open(\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=\" + p.lat + \",\" + p.lon, \"_blank\"); }\n    } else if (t.hasAttribute(\"data-show\")) {\n      var pid = t.getAttribute(\"data-show\");\n      onMap(function (m) { m.flyTo(pid, 15); });\n    } else if (t.hasAttribute(\"data-route\")) {\n      var rid = t.getAttribute(\"data-route\");\n      onMap(function (m) { m.highlightRoute(rid); });\n    } else if (t.hasAttribute(\"data-day-map\")) {\n      var date = t.getAttribute(\"data-day-map\");\n      $(\"#map-day\").value = date;\n      onMap(function (m) { m.setDay(date); });\n    } else if (t.hasAttribute(\"data-filter\")) {\n      placeFilter = t.getAttribute(\"data-filter\");\n      renderPlaces();\n    } else if (W && t.tagName === \"A\") {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      W.openExternal(t.href);\n    }\n  });\n  window.addEventListener(\"hashchange\", route);\n\n  function updateNet() {\n    var online = W ? W.isOnline() : navigator.onLine;\n    $(\"#net\").hidden = online;\n  }\n  window.addEventListener(\"online\", updateNet);\n  window.addEventListener(\"offline\", updateNet);\n\n  // ---------- boot ----------\n  var load = W ? W.manifest() : fetch(\"manifest.json\").then(function (r) { return r.json(); });\n  load.then(function (m) {\n    M = m;\n    M.places.forEach(function (p) { placesById[p.id] = p; });\n    M.routes.forEach(function (r) { routesById[r.id] = r; });\n    document.title = M.title;\n    $(\"#trip-title\").textContent = M.title;\n    $(\"#trip-dates\").textContent = fmtDate(M.start_date) + \" – \" + fmtDate(M.end_date, { year: \"numeric\" });\n    renderToday();\n    renderPlan();\n    renderPlaces();\n    renderGuide();\n    renderMapDays();\n    updateNet();\n    route();\n    // Keep Today fresh while the app stays open.\n    setInterval(function () { if (!$(\"#tab-today\").hidden) renderToday(); }, 60000);\n  }).catch(function (e) {\n    $(\"#app\").innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Could not load this trip: ' + esc(e.message) + \"</p>\";\n  });\n})();\n","assets/style.css":"/* Waypack base template — mobile-first, one-handed, readable at arm's length. */\n:root {\n  --bg: #f6f7f9;\n  --surface: #ffffff;\n  --surface-2: #eef1f5;\n  --text: #0f172a;\n  --muted: #5b6577;\n  --line: #dde2ea;\n  --accent: #1d6fe0;\n  --accent-ink: #ffffff;\n  --ok: #15803d;\n  --warn: #b45309;\n  --danger: #c81e1e;\n  --radius: 14px;\n  --tap: 48px;\n  --tabbar-h: 64px;\n  --font: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, \"Noto Sans\", system-ui, sans-serif;\n  color-scheme: light dark;\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root {\n    --bg: #0b1120;\n    --surface: #141c2f;\n    --surface-2: #1c2640;\n    --text: #e8edf6;\n    --muted: #9aa6bb;\n    --line: #26314a;\n    --accent: #5b9bff;\n    --accent-ink: #06122a;\n    --ok: #4ade80;\n    --warn: #fbbf24;\n    --danger: #f87171;\n  }\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nhtml { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-padding-top: 72px; }\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  font: 17px/1.5 var(--font);\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  padding-bottom: calc(var(--tabbar-h) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 12px);\n}\nh1, h2, h3 { line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 .4em; }\nh2 { font-size: 1.2rem; }\nh3 { font-size: 1.02rem; margin-top: 1em; }\np { margin: 0 0 .75em; }\na { color: var(--accent); }\n.muted { color: var(--muted); }\nsmall { font-size: .85rem; }\n\n/* Top bar */\n.topbar {\n  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10;\n  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;\n  padding: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top) + 10px) 16px 10px;\n  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 88%, transparent);\n  backdrop-filter: saturate(1.4) blur(12px);\n  -webkit-backdrop-filter: saturate(1.4) blur(12px);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);\n}\n.topbar-inner { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }\n.topbar h1 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }\n.topbar p { margin: 0; font-size: .85rem; }\n.net { font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--muted); }\n\nmain { padding: 12px 12px 0; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }\n.tab[hidden] { display: none !important; }\n\n/* Cards */\n.card {\n  background: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: var(--radius);\n  padding: 16px;\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\n}\n.card > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n\n/* Today hero */\n.hero { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); border: 0; }\n.hero .label { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; opacity: .85; }\n.hero h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; margin: .2em 0; }\n.hero .when { font-weight: 600; opacity: .95; }\n.hero .btn { background: var(--accent-ink); color: var(--accent); }\n\n/* Buttons */\n.btn {\n  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 6px;\n  min-height: var(--tap); padding: 10px 16px;\n  border: 0; border-radius: 12px;\n  background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink);\n  font: 600 1rem var(--font); text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer;\n}\n.btn.secondary { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--text); }\n.btn.small { min-height: 44px; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: .92rem; }\n.btn-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 10px; }\n\n/* Timeline */\n.day { margin-bottom: 18px; }\n.day-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px; padding: 4px 4px 8px; }\n.day-head h2 { margin: 0; }\n.items { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n.item {\n  display: grid; grid-template-columns: 62px 1fr; gap: 10px;\n  background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);\n  padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n.item.now { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: -1px; }\n.item.done { opacity: .55; }\n.item .time { font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: .95rem; }\n.item .time small { display: block; font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); }\n.item h3 { margin: 0 0 2px; font-size: 1.02rem; }\n.item p { margin: 4px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }\n.tag { display: inline-block; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--muted); margin-right: 4px; }\n.day-notes { background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 12px 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }\n\n/* Places */\n.filters, .chips { display: flex; gap: 8px; overflow-x: auto; padding: 2px 0 10px; scrollbar-width: none; }\n.filters::-webkit-scrollbar, .chips::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }\n.filters button, .chips a {\n  flex: none; min-height: 40px; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  background: var(--surface); color: var(--text); font: 600 .9rem var(--font); text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer;\n}\n.filters button[aria-pressed=\"true\"] { background: var(--text); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--text); }\n.place { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr; gap: 12px; }\n.place .dot { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 20px; }\n.place h3 { margin: 0; }\n.place .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; }\n\n/* Map */\n.tab-map { position: relative; }\n.map { height: calc(100dvh - 190px); min-height: 320px; border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.map-tools { margin-bottom: 8px; }\nselect { min-height: 44px; width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); color: var(--text); font: 1rem var(--font); padding: 8px 12px; }\n\n/* Lists, tables */\n.kv { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }\n.kv li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.kv li:first-child { border-top: 0; }\n.kv span { color: var(--muted); }\n.kv b { text-align: right; }\n.table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.table th, .table td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 4px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.table .num { text-align: right; }\n.link-list a { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; min-height: var(--tap); padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }\n.link-list a::after { content: \"↗\"; color: var(--muted); }\n.link-list a:first-child { border-top: 0; }\n.checklist { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }\n.checklist li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: var(--tap); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); cursor: pointer; user-select: none; }\n.checklist li:first-child { border-top: 0; }\n.checklist li::before { content: \"\"; flex: none; width: 24px; height: 24px; border-radius: 7px; border: 2px solid var(--line); }\n.checklist li.checked { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: line-through; }\n.checklist li.checked::before { background: var(--ok); border-color: var(--ok); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 3px var(--surface); }\ndetails { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 8px 0; }\ndetails summary { min-height: 40px; display: flex; align-items: center; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }\n.emergency-num { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 6px 0; }\n.emergency-num a { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.1rem; }\n.callout { border-left: 4px solid var(--warn); background: var(--surface-2); padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 8px 0; }\n.empty { text-align: center; color: var(--muted); padding: 32px 16px; }\n\n/* Tab bar */\n.tabbar {\n  position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 20;\n  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);\n  height: calc(var(--tabbar-h) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));\n  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);\n  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 92%, transparent);\n  backdrop-filter: saturate(1.4) blur(14px);\n  -webkit-backdrop-filter: saturate(1.4) blur(14px);\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);\n}\n.tabbar a {\n  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 2px;\n  color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; font-size: .74rem; font-weight: 600;\n}\n.tabbar a span { font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1; }\n.tabbar a[aria-current=\"page\"] { color: var(--accent); }\n\n@media (min-width: 760px) {\n  body { font-size: 16px; }\n  .map { height: calc(100vh - 200px); }\n}\n@media print {\n  .tabbar, .topbar, .tab-map, .btn, .filters { display: none !important; }\n  .tab[hidden] { display: block !important; }\n  .card, .item { break-inside: avoid; }\n}\n","index.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n  <meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\n  <title>Trip</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/style.css\">\n  <!-- Waypack SDK: offline maps, Navigate buttons, share. Served by the app; never bundle MapLibre yourself. -->\n  <script src=\"/__waypack/sdk/v1/waypack.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <header class=\"topbar\">\n    <div class=\"topbar-inner\">\n      <h1 id=\"trip-title\">Trip</h1>\n      <p id=\"trip-dates\" class=\"muted\"></p>\n    </div>\n    <span id=\"net\" class=\"net\" hidden>Offline</span>\n  </header>\n\n  <main id=\"app\">\n    <!-- Rendered from manifest.json by assets/app.js -->\n    <section id=\"tab-today\" class=\"tab\" data-tab=\"today\"></section>\n    <section id=\"tab-plan\" class=\"tab\" data-tab=\"plan\" hidden></section>\n    <section id=\"tab-map\" class=\"tab tab-map\" data-tab=\"map\" hidden>\n      <div class=\"map-tools\">\n        <select id=\"map-day\" aria-label=\"Show day on map\"><option value=\"\">All days</option></select>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"map\" class=\"map\"></div>\n    </section>\n    <section id=\"tab-places\" class=\"tab\" data-tab=\"places\" hidden></section>\n\n    <!-- ===================================================================\n         GUIDE — authored by the agent as plain HTML. Keep every section\n         (write \"N/A — reason\" rather than deleting one). Cards with\n         class=\"card\" get consistent styling. Use <details> for long lists.\n         =================================================================== -->\n    <section id=\"tab-guide\" class=\"tab\" data-tab=\"guide\" hidden>\n      <nav class=\"chips\" aria-label=\"Guide sections\">\n        <a href=\"#g-overview\">Overview</a><a href=\"#g-conditions\">Conditions</a><a href=\"#g-safety\">Safety</a>\n        <a href=\"#g-packing\">Packing</a><a href=\"#g-budget\">Budget</a><a href=\"#g-backup\">Backup plans</a><a href=\"#g-offline\">Offline prep</a>\n      </nav>\n\n      <article id=\"g-overview\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Overview</h2>\n        <p>SAMPLE — replace with a one-screen summary: who's going, the shape of each day, and the reservations that matter.</p>\n        <ul class=\"kv\">\n          <li><span>Lodging</span><b>Yosemite Valley Lodge · Conf. #SAMPLE</b></li>\n          <li><span>Park entry</span><b>Reservation may be required — verify</b></li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-conditions\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Conditions &amp; live checks</h2>\n        <p>Seasonal risks to plan around. Conditions change — check the links below before leaving and whenever you get signal.</p>\n        <div id=\"live-checks\" class=\"link-list\"><!-- filled from manifest.live_checks --></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-safety\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Emergency &amp; safety</h2>\n        <div id=\"emergency\"><!-- filled from manifest.emergency --></div>\n        <p>Cell service is limited in most of the valley outside Yosemite Village.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-packing\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Packing list</h2>\n        <ul class=\"checklist\" data-store=\"packing\">\n          <li>Layers + rain shell</li>\n          <li>Headlamp</li>\n          <li>Water bottles</li>\n          <li>Power bank (charged)</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-budget\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Budget</h2>\n        <table class=\"table\">\n          <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th class=\"num\">Estimate</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td>Lodging (1 night)</td><td class=\"num\">$300</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Park entry</td><td class=\"num\">$35</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Food</td><td class=\"num\">$120</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n          <tfoot><tr><th>Total</th><th class=\"num\">≈ $455</th></tr></tfoot>\n        </table>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-backup\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Backup plans</h2>\n        <h3>If it rains</h3>\n        <p>Visitor center exhibits and the Ansel Adams Gallery.</p>\n        <h3>If a trail is closed</h3>\n        <p>Walk the flat valley loop instead.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article id=\"g-offline\" class=\"card\">\n        <h2>Offline prep</h2>\n        <ul class=\"checklist\" data-store=\"offline\">\n          <li>Download this trip in Waypack (map included)</li>\n          <li>Download a Google/Apple Maps offline area for the drive</li>\n          <li>Charge phones and power banks</li>\n          <li>Screenshot or print key confirmations</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Optional rich notes per day: app.js moves each block into that day in the Plan tab. -->\n    <div hidden>\n      <div data-day-notes=\"2026-06-12\"><p>Rich per-day notes (tips, photos, why this order) go here.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  <nav class=\"tabbar\" aria-label=\"Sections\">\n    <a href=\"#today\" data-go=\"today\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">◎</span>Today</a>\n    <a href=\"#plan\" data-go=\"plan\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">☰</span>Plan</a>\n    <a href=\"#map\" data-go=\"map\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">⌖</span>Map</a>\n    <a href=\"#places\" data-go=\"places\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">◉</span>Places</a>\n    <a href=\"#guide\" data-go=\"guide\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">✦</span>Guide</a>\n  </nav>\n\n  <script src=\"assets/app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","manifest.json":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"sdk_version\": \"1\",\n  \"trip_id\": null,\n  \"title\": \"SAMPLE — Yosemite Valley Overnight\",\n  \"summary\": \"Template sample. Replace every field with researched data; coordinates must come from the geocode tool and route geometry from compute_route.\",\n  \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\",\n  \"start_date\": \"2026-06-12\",\n  \"end_date\": \"2026-06-13\",\n  \"travelers\": { \"adults\": 2, \"children\": [] },\n  \"nav_app\": \"google\",\n  \"map\": { \"bbox\": [-119.66, 37.70, -119.52, 37.77], \"max_zoom\": 15, \"extra_areas\": [] },\n  \"places\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"lodge-yvl\",\n      \"name\": \"Yosemite Valley Lodge\",\n      \"category\": \"lodging\",\n      \"lat\": 37.7425, \"lon\": -119.5965,\n      \"address\": \"9006 Yosemite Lodge Dr, Yosemite Valley, CA 95389\",\n      \"notes\": \"SAMPLE. Check-in 4pm, check-out 11am. Confirmation #SAMPLE.\",\n      \"links\": [{ \"label\": \"Lodge website\", \"url\": \"https://www.travelyosemite.com/\" }]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"trailhead-lower-falls\",\n      \"name\": \"Lower Yosemite Fall Trailhead\",\n      \"category\": \"trailhead\",\n      \"lat\": 37.7466, \"lon\": -119.5960,\n      \"notes\": \"1 mi paved loop, stroller-friendly.\",\n      \"hours\": \"24 h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"village-store\",\n      \"name\": \"Yosemite Village Store\",\n      \"category\": \"shopping\",\n      \"lat\": 37.7485, \"lon\": -119.5870,\n      \"hours\": \"8am–8pm (verify)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"clinic\",\n      \"name\": \"Yosemite Medical Clinic (verify status)\",\n      \"category\": \"medical\",\n      \"lat\": 37.7468, \"lon\": -119.5813\n    }\n  ],\n  \"routes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"r-lodge-falls\",\n      \"name\": \"Lodge → Lower Yosemite Fall\",\n      \"mode\": \"walking\",\n      \"from\": \"lodge-yvl\", \"to\": \"trailhead-lower-falls\",\n      \"distance_m\": 700, \"duration_s\": 600,\n      \"geometry\": { \"type\": \"LineString\", \"coordinates\": [[-119.5965, 37.7425], [-119.5968, 37.7440], [-119.5964, 37.7455], [-119.5960, 37.7466]] },\n      \"notes\": \"SAMPLE geometry — use compute_route for real paths.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"days\": [\n    {\n      \"date\": \"2026-06-12\",\n      \"title\": \"Arrive & waterfalls\",\n      \"items\": [\n        { \"time\": \"15:00\", \"end_time\": \"16:00\", \"title\": \"Check in\", \"place_id\": \"lodge-yvl\", \"kind\": \"lodging\" },\n        { \"time\": \"16:30\", \"end_time\": \"17:30\", \"title\": \"Walk to Lower Yosemite Fall\", \"place_id\": \"trailhead-lower-falls\", \"route_id\": \"r-lodge-falls\", \"kind\": \"activity\" },\n        { \"time\": \"18:00\", \"title\": \"Groceries for tomorrow\", \"place_id\": \"village-store\", \"kind\": \"other\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"date\": \"2026-06-13\",\n      \"title\": \"Morning walk & depart\",\n      \"items\": [\n        { \"time\": \"08:00\", \"title\": \"Breakfast\", \"kind\": \"meal\" },\n        { \"time\": \"11:00\", \"title\": \"Check out\", \"place_id\": \"lodge-yvl\", \"kind\": \"lodging\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"live_checks\": [\n    { \"label\": \"Yosemite current conditions (NPS)\", \"url\": \"https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/conditions.htm\" },\n    { \"label\": \"Caltrans QuickMap road conditions\", \"url\": \"https://quickmap.dot.ca.gov/\" }\n  ],\n  \"emergency\": {\n    \"numbers\": [{ \"label\": \"Emergency\", \"value\": \"911\" }],\n    \"notes\": \"SAMPLE — list the nearest hospital and ranger station here.\",\n    \"places\": [\"clinic\"]\n  },\n  \"offline_notes\": \"Download this trip in Waypack before leaving home.\"\n}\n"}} as const;
